# TARGET ARCHITECTURE: x86_64 | v0.16.4 | azure/almalinux9
# Enterprise Linux Audit v0.16.4  |  [azure/almalinux9]
# Tier: tier-2-core-security
# Purpose: account security, authentication and credential surfaces
# Source/authority: Enterprise SOC/IR minimum
# Architecture: x86_64 (b64 native, b32 compatibility); use aarch64/ subprofile for ARM64.
# Release state: engineering candidate; NOT independently certified STIG compliant.


-a always,exit -F arch=b64 -F dir=/etc/pam.d -F perm=wa -k t2_auth_change
# OPTIONAL SSH key and security directories, if present:
# -a always,exit -F arch=b64 -F dir=/etc/ssh -F perm=wa -k t2_ssh_change
# -a always,exit -F arch=b64 -F dir=/etc/security -F perm=wa -k t2_auth_change
# Local credential files below home directories require per-host targeting; do not audit all home reads.
